-             :plan "On a fresh agent (r3-probe-b, branch :agent-2559040ff3c5, default 2026-10-12) ONE request `(ns r3b.probe (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is]]))` `(defmulti area :shape)` `(defmethod area :sq [{:keys [s]}] (* s s))` `(deftest t-multi (is (= 4 (area {:shape :sq :s 2}))))` answers every value, then the reaching step reports `t-multi` errored (`:seon.test.failure/reports` \"The admitted identity has no executable test Var.\") and records error 500ddeeeca094b0ccd26f74c3bd90c64c2775fa762f11344b7f8b9de5ec9aec1 (`seon.sci.eval/acquisition-refusal`, \"Program row could not be installed\"); the refusal on `(seon.sci.eval/program-context (seon.db/db))` names row `[:seon.test/sym r3b.probe/t-multi]`, cause \"Unable to resolve symbol: area\". The cause is the producer of the branch's rows, not acquisition: `seon.turn.batch/write-entity` keeps `area` private (`:not-a-function`, a `clojure.lang.MultiFn` is not `fn?`) and `seon.turn.batch/derive-form` receives no write for the `defmethod`, so the acquired program holds a test calling a name no row declares, and every later request reruns the errored test (test-step 490 ms). Fixed with `seon.sci.eval/a-defmethod-is-a-declaration-on-a-branch` (options in the evidence): the multimethod and its methods become rows, so acquisition installs both. Proof: the `seon.sci.eval-test` deftest `a-multimethod-and-its-test-in-one-request-acquire-on-a-branch` the implementer writes first submits those four forms in one request on a fresh branch and asserts the program context's acquisition has no refusal and `t-multi` passes. Read `seon.sci.eval/install-selected!` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/r3-notes.md`."}
