  #:seon.task{:name "the-loaded-commit-is-materialized-on-every-call"
              :plan "`seon.sci.eval/loaded-program` opens the loaded commit with `datahike.api/commit-as-db` on every call, uncached: the P1 lane (branch-head-p1, 2026-10-15) measured about 550 MB allocated per overlay probe. A commit is immutable, so the materialized value is a function of the store and the commit id (`seon.sci.eval/store-identity`, `seon.sci.eval/loaded-commit-id`) plus the carried projection it is stamped with (`seon.db/carried-projection`). Done when it is one `seon.cache` kind keyed by that content (as `seon.sci.eval/loaded-digests` is), a second `loaded-program` call of the same commit allocates under 1 MB in a `seon.profile/measure` proof parent vs change, and `seon.db/commit-database` (the same open, in `seon.cluster.registry`) shares it. Weigh the entry honestly: the value holds index roots whose nodes Datahike's own cache owns."}
